1
00:00:00,022 --> 00:00:01,817
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,421
Resgrid brings dispatch, people,
apparatus, and department

3
00:00:06,427 --> 00:00:08,609
management into a connected system.

4
00:00:08,813 --> 00:00:13,742
This series explains what each feature
does, how to prepare it, and how to tell

5
00:00:13,742 --> 00:00:15,706
whether it is helping your department.

6
00:00:16,511 --> 00:00:21,715
Picture a fictional department with two
stations, an engine, and a rescue unit.

7
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:27,408
First, administrators organize members,
groups, roles, and units.

8
00:00:27,624 --> 00:00:31,927
A dispatcher creates a training call and
selects the intended resources.

9
00:00:32,108 --> 00:00:34,753
Members respond through their assigned
devices.

10
00:00:34,973 --> 00:00:38,890
After closeout, officers complete records
and follow up on

11
00:00:38,890 --> 00:00:41,667
equipment, supplies, and staffing.

12
00:00:42,494 --> 00:00:44,019
Start with the foundation.

13
00:00:44,266 --> 00:00:46,755
Set the department address and time zone.

14
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:51,791
Build the roster, home stations, personnel
roles, and unit types.

15
00:00:51,988 --> 00:00:55,520
Review who can dispatch, manage
information, and

16
00:00:55,524 --> 00:00:57,080
administer the department.

17
00:00:57,239 --> 00:01:01,352
Prepare account recovery as you set up
stronger sign-in protections.

18
00:01:01,566 --> 00:01:07,071
These choices influence later schedules,
recipients, maps, and reports.

19
00:01:07,929 --> 00:01:13,906
For operations, learn call intake, types,
priorities, recipient routing,

20
00:01:14,081 --> 00:01:16,694
run cards, and response statuses.

21
00:01:16,909 --> 00:01:19,701
Mapping adds location and site context.

22
00:01:19,887 --> 00:01:24,031
Messaging and notification rules keep the
intended audience informed.

23
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:27,360
Verify communications on actual devices.

24
00:01:27,580 --> 00:01:30,446
A saved call or provider handoff is
different from

25
00:01:30,446 --> 00:01:32,280
confirmed receipt by a member.

26
00:01:33,056 --> 00:01:35,995
Between calls, shifts help plan coverage.

27
00:01:36,203 --> 00:01:40,290
Training and certification records make
learning and renewal work visible.

28
00:01:40,481 --> 00:01:42,925
Checklists record routine inspections.

29
00:01:43,141 --> 00:01:47,310
Maintenance gives defects an owner and a
documented repair process.

30
00:01:47,475 --> 00:01:50,371
Inventory records where equipment and
supplies are

31
00:01:50,371 --> 00:01:52,747
stored, issued, and replenished.

32
00:01:52,967 --> 00:01:57,607
Documents, contacts, protocols, and
calendars give members

33
00:01:57,609 --> 00:01:59,075
a shared reference point.

34
00:01:59,868 --> 00:02:04,292
Records connect incident reporting,
prevention, investigation,

35
00:02:04,473 --> 00:02:07,069
evidence, review, and disclosure.

36
00:02:07,246 --> 00:02:10,266
Deployments keep extended response
activity and

37
00:02:10,266 --> 00:02:12,065
supporting documents together.

38
00:02:12,246 --> 00:02:16,465
Business Operations adds commercial and
costing workflows where enabled.

39
00:02:16,654 --> 00:02:21,673
Teach the source activity, review
decisions, and recorded outcomes together,

40
00:02:21,825 --> 00:02:26,722
rather than treating an export or prepared
claim as a completed external submission.

41
00:02:27,576 --> 00:02:32,037
Feature availability depends on the
deployed release and department access.

42
00:02:32,279 --> 00:02:36,431
Some features need an enabled module, a
permission, an add-on,

43
00:02:36,609 --> 00:02:38,139
or protection enrollment.

44
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:41,431
The source catalog marks Enhanced AI as
planned.

45
00:02:41,581 --> 00:02:44,286
Buying an add-on is separate from
configuring it.

46
00:02:44,513 --> 00:02:47,833
Setup Report helps review configuration
evidence;

47
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:52,716
it does not prove that every operational
workflow or notification has succeeded.

48
00:02:53,514 --> 00:02:57,792
Choose the learning path that matches your
responsibility: administrator,

49
00:02:57,947 --> 00:03:00,653
dispatcher, member, or specialist.

50
00:03:00,817 --> 00:03:05,169
Each chapter explains a department
problem, the relevant features,

51
00:03:05,397 --> 00:03:08,189
setup decisions, and a practice task.

52
00:03:08,379 --> 00:03:11,598
These illustrated lessons are based on the
current source.

53
00:03:11,815 --> 00:03:16,590
Live screen walkthroughs will be recorded
against a verified demo department, with

54
00:03:16,598 --> 00:03:19,110
